1. docker pull image_name 
is used to download container images from a registry (such as Docker Hub) to your local machine.

2. docker images
command (and its modern alias docker image ls) is primarily used to list all top-level Docker images currently stored on your local system. 

3. docker run image_name/id
is used to create and start a new container from a specific Docker image. It is the primary command for launching containerized applications.

4. docker run -it <image_name/id>  
is used to create and start a new container from a specific image and interact with it immediately through a terminal.

5. docker start container_name/id
is used to restart one or more stopped containers.

6. docker stop container_name/id
is used to gracefully shut down one or more running containers.

7. docker ps -a
is used to list all Docker containers on your system, regardless of their current state.

8. docker ps
is is used to list only running container

9. docker rmi image_name/id
(shorthand for remove miage) is used to delete one or more Docker images from your local host. but you must delete the container first that you had created using this image.

10. docker rm container_name/id
is used to remove one or more containers from a Docker host. Removing a container deletes its execution environment, process metadata, and internal filesystem changes, freeing up system resources.

11. docker pull image_name:version
is used to download a specific version (tag) of a container image from a registry, such as Docker Hub, to your local machine.

12. docker run -d image_name/id 
is used to create and start a new container from a specified image in detached mode. 
-d (or --detach): This flag runs the container in the background. This means the container starts up, but your terminal remains free for other tasks instead of being "attached" to the container's output.

13. docker run -e env_variable=value image_name/id 
is used to create and start a new container from a specific image while injecting an environment variable into that container's runtime environment.

14. docker run --name custom_name image_name/id
is used to launch a new Docker container from a specified image and assign it a specific, memorable name. 

15. docker run -p host_port:container_port image_name/id
is used to create and start a new container while mapping a port from your physical computer (host) to a port inside the container.

16. docker logs container_name/id
is used to retrieve, view, or stream the standard output (stdout) and standard error (stderr) generated by a running or stopped Docker container.

17. docker exec -it container_id /bin/bash or /bin/sh
is used to start a new interactive Bash shell session inside a Docker container that is already running.
docker exec: Tells Docker to run a new command in an existing, running container.

18. docker container prune
is used to remove all stopped containers from your system.

19. docker image prune
is primarily used to remove unused images from your local Docker host to reclaim disk space.











